27
00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:12.630
But first, I want us to share about an amazing dinner party that we were just at recently

28
00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.010
that I'm still delighted by.

29
00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:20.470
It was one of those dinner parties where it was a humongous, huge table, like a giant,

30
00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.710
long rectangle of just such fun people.

31
00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:27.710
There were probably, what, like it was 26 of us at a restaurant.

32
00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:29.350
We got a little private room.

33
00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:35.410
And it was to celebrate the wrap of Lee's movie, New Year's Rev.

34
00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:36.070
Yeah.

35
00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:37.830
The cast was there.

36
00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.950
A bunch of the producers were there.

37
00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:40.930
Some of the crew.

38
00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:41.750
Yeah.

39
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:45.210
So we had just finished shooting at the Palladium with Green Day.

40
00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:46.930
And we all go out to dinner.

41
00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.110
And Angela, you came up for it.

42
00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:51.010
And Bobby Lee was there.

43
00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:51.430
Yeah.

44
00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:55.830
And the two of you took over this dinner party.

45
00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:57.670
Well, it was amazing.

46
00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:58.630
Here's the thing.

47
00:01:58.730 --> 00:01:59.130
Here's the thing.

48
00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:03.130
We sat right in the middle of this long table.

49
00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:03.550
Yes.

50
00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:05.790
And you and Lee were right across from us.

51
00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:07.950
And Bobby and I kind of split the table.

52
00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.850
To his right were all the actors.

53
00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:13.070
And to the left were a lot of the crew and producers.

54
00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:13.530
Yeah.

55
00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:16.190
And him and I were chatting and chatting and chatting.

56
00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:18.090
And we would sort of engage with the actors.

57
00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:22.410
And then I said to him, I kind of feel bad that we're not talking to anyone on the left

58
00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:23.150
side of the table.

59
00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:25.590
And he sort of threw down this gauntlet.

60
00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:26.450
He was like, oh, no, no.

61
00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:27.790
He goes, you can't get in there.

62
00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:28.910
Look, they're all talking to each other.

63
00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:29.750
They don't want to talk to you.

64
00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:30.610
You can't get in there.

65
00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:32.650
Good luck getting in that conversation.

66
00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:34.110
And I said, oh, yeah?

67
00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:37.310
And he was like, yeah, I dare you try to get in that conversation.

68
00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:43.390
And so I immediately stood up and I took my fork to my wine glass and went, clink, clink, clink, clink.

69
00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:47.330
You guys, she stood up and did the thing where you're going to do a toaSt.

70
00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:48.610
Like at a wedding.

71
00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:49.770
It was so funny.

72
00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.250
The whole room goes silent.

73
00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:51.890
Silent.

74
00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:54.090
And I'm thinking, what is she doing?

75
00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.270
And you, it was so funny, Angela.

76
00:02:56.630 --> 00:03:01.750
Angela goes, everyone, I worked three days on this film.

77
00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:07.290
And so it seems only fitting that I should speak, that I should give a toaSt.

78
00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:09.150
And it was so funny.

79
00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:12.430
And you gave a very funny toast, a very sweet toast as well.

80
00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:12.710
I did.

81
00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:16.610
I basically was like, this was such a wonderful project to be a part of.

82
00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:22.390
Lee, you did such an amazing job, like just setting the tone for this creative experience.

83
00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:27.250
And so when I sat down, the group to the left looks at me and goes, oh.

84
00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:30.630
And one of the producers was like, thank you so much for saying that.

85
00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:33.550
And look, I am in now with the left side of the table.

86
00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:35.430
And I look over at Bobby like, uh-huh.

87
00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:36.890
And he goes, damn it.

88
00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:38.350
And he pops up.

89
00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.130
And he does a clink, clink, clink.

90
00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.190
And then he goes, I have a toaSt.

91
00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:43.790
And I'm going to say it in Korean.

92
00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:44.910
Yes.

93
00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.010
And then we were all like, oh.

94
00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:49.350
And he does his toaSt.

95
00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:50.310
And he sits down.

96
00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:52.150
And then Angela.

97
00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:54.130
I immediately pop back up.

98
00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:55.650
And I go, clink, clink, clink.

99
00:03:55.750 --> 00:04:00.290
And I said, I lived in Indonesia for 12 years, from ages 2 to 14.

100
00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.810
And I am now going to give a toast in Indonesian.

101
00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:04.350
And everyone was like, wah!

102
00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:06.870
It was so great.

103
00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:09.370
And then Ignacio, one of the actors, stands up.

104
00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:10.790
He gives a speech in Spanish.

105
00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.450
And then the production designer, Adam, stands up.

106
00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:14.890
He gives a speech in Italian.

107
00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:20.750
Guys, all I can say was this dueling speeches was one of the highlights of the dinner.

108
00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:22.370
Angela kicked it all off.

109
00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.190
It was just such a fun night.

110
00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:25.470
It was really fun.

111
00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:29.130
Well, that is an example of an amazing dinner party.

112
00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:29.850
That was fun.

113
00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:34.530
And there's nothing more fun than an amazing dinner party, which I think is why when a

