275
00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:19.430
To the surprise of no one, they are no longer together.

276
00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:21.610
O-M-G.

277
00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:26.830
They called the co-worker at the dinner party on speakerphone.

278
00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:29.050
I mean, that's insane.

279
00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:31.930
But my favorite part of this letter is the dinner.

280
00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:33.150
The chicken legs.

281
00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:34.250
With no sides.

282
00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:34.930
No sides.

283
00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:35.970
What is this meal?

284
00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:36.850
I don't know.

285
00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:38.630
Oh, Shannon, that made me laugh.

286
00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:43.030
Well, lack of food was a common theme in your dinner party horror stories.

287
00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:45.970
Liz Kaye from Philadelphia, Pennsylvania said,

288
00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:52.310
We were invited over for a cookout and they had no ketchup and thought nothing wrong with this.

289
00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:58.550
And they only served three hot dogs and two burgers and one steak for five adults.

290
00:12:59.330 --> 00:12:59.890
What?

291
00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:01.990
How do you divide up that food?

292
00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:02.810
How do you divide up?

293
00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:04.770
Like, what if everyone wanted a hot dog?

294
00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:07.070
I guess you could cut them in half.

295
00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:08.830
Everyone could get half a hot dog.

296
00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:09.650
With no ketchup.

297
00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:12.550
And some steak and two burgers.

298
00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.350
Again, no sides.

299
00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:15.690
No sides.

300
00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:18.590
We also got a fan story from Emily R.

301
00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:20.610
in Tulsa, Oklahoma, who said,

302
00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:25.370
When I was a kid, my parents hauled my sister and I to a neighbor's dinner party.

303
00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:29.130
We arrived around five, thinking we'd be eating at six.

304
00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:36.010
We learned we'd be having ribs for dinner, but they were behind schedule and we didn't eat until almost 9 p.m.

305
00:13:36.090 --> 00:13:36.630
Oh, my gosh.

306
00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:38.130
What does that remind you of?

307
00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:39.450
Jan's osapuka.

308
00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:45.010
When dinner was served, they had enough for two ribs per person.

309
00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:49.930
My sister and I quickly ate our portion and then sat in hangry moods.

310
00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:50.790
No sides.

311
00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:51.850
No sides again.

312
00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:59.470
The brother of the host then stood up, walked around the table, collecting everyone's rib bones off their plates,

313
00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:05.110
and proceeded to suck the already eaten off of rib bones to get every last morsel.

314
00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:08.030
We had never met this man in our life.

315
00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.850
I can't eat ribs anymore.

316
00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:12.070
I'm so disgusted by this memory.

317
00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:13.950
He got everyone's ribs?

318
00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:15.210
What?

319
00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:16.430
I don't know.

320
00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:18.350
And sat there and sucked on them?

321
00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:23.830
You know, Angela, one of my big fears when I'm throwing a dinner party is that I'm not going to have enough food.

322
00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:28.110
And I cannot tell you how many times I have planned the food.

323
00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:35.190
And then, like, in the last hour before the party is supposed to start, I send Lee to the store to buy more food.

324
00:14:35.190 --> 00:14:38.790
And I panic, and then I end up with way too much food at the end.

325
00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:40.550
Is this—have you ever done this?

326
00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:42.750
I mean, I think we always do this.

327
00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:44.090
I think we're always worried.

328
00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:48.450
You know where I go overboard is, like, the munchies before the dinner.

329
00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:50.610
Like, Josh is always like, babe, stop.

330
00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:52.490
Because I'm like, okay, I have mixed nuts.

331
00:14:52.510 --> 00:14:53.150
I have hummus.

332
00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:54.290
I have a cheese plate.

333
00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:56.170
I have some salami.

334
00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:57.550
I have a dip.

335
00:14:57.930 --> 00:14:59.050
I have three more dips.

336
00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.990
Oh, maybe we should have something sweet.

337
00:15:01.350 --> 00:15:03.590
He's like, stop with the munchies.

338
00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:09.130
Well, something I know about going to a party at your house is that I am going to arrive to food.

339
00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:09.910
Oh, yeah.

340
00:15:09.910 --> 00:15:13.970
So you are very good at having out that, like, pre-dinner moment.

341
00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:14.930
Oh, no, yeah.

342
00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:17.930
No, I want food the minute I walk in your house.

343
00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:23.330
Like, so if you invite me over, if you don't have food out right away, I'm going to have a granola bar in my bag.

344
00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:24.330
Are you Pam?

345
00:15:24.430 --> 00:15:24.870
I'm Pam.

346
00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:26.970
I don't care what they think about me.

347
00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:27.810
I just want to eat.

348
00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:29.030
All right.

349
00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:31.890
We've got this other letter from Hannah in Oregon.

350
00:15:32.330 --> 00:15:33.590
Hannah wrote in and said,

351
00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:40.710
A few years ago, I went to a Hanukkah party where I met my partner's co-worker, who was the host for the first time.

352
00:15:41.150 --> 00:15:44.590
The host was cooking glazed carrots before the meal started.

353
00:15:44.830 --> 00:15:53.670
I was standing in the kitchen chatting with them when, out of nowhere, they pulled a carrot out of the cooking pot with their bare fingers

354
00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:55.690
and bit it in half.

355
00:15:55.690 --> 00:16:04.530
But instead of eating the second half of the carrot, I watched in horror as they put the half-eaten carrot back in the pot.

356
00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:05.530
No, no.

357
00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:08.590
And Hannah's like, were they trying to check for doneness?

358
00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:09.950
I mean, what the heck?

359
00:16:10.390 --> 00:16:16.250
Then, then Hannah says, after they put the half-eaten carrot back in the pot, they licked their fingers.

360
00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:16.730
No.

361
00:16:16.730 --> 00:16:23.970
I stood there frozen trying to process what just happened, but before I could form a complete thought, the host did it again.

362
00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:24.890
Oh, my gosh.

363
00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:25.990
With a new carrot.

364
00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:32.170
They stuck their pre-licked fingers back in the pot, grabbed a new carrot, bit it in half,

365
00:16:32.330 --> 00:16:36.890
and then dropped the remaining half of the carrot back in the pot and stirred it all together.

366
00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:40.430
Hannah says, I immediately made an excuse to step out.

367
00:16:40.590 --> 00:16:43.550
I found my partner and frantically whispered, don't eat the carrots.

368
00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:46.710
I want to know that car ride home.

369
00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:48.150
I need to know.

370
00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:48.730
I know.

371
00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:51.670
Hannah says, needless to say, we did not eat the carrots.

372
00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:55.770
We left before nine, and we did not go back the next year for many other reasons.

373
00:16:56.210 --> 00:17:04.010
And lady, this made me think of the moment in dinner party when Michael comes back from the bathroom and Jan asks if he washed his hands.

374
00:17:04.150 --> 00:17:04.430
Yes.

375
00:17:04.630 --> 00:17:10.670
And he says yes, but then he whispers to Jim and Pam no, and he like touches everything on the appetizer plate.

376
00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:14.850
I mean, I know I just described it, but it's a little longer than the superfan episode.

377
00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:15.490
