00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:24.750
I didn't really wash my hands.

381
00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:26.530
Oh, what have we here?

382
00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:29.010
This looks delicious.

383
00:17:29.350 --> 00:17:29.810
Those are your hands.

384
00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:33.650
But they need to be presented royally.

385
00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:34.130
Anyone?

386
00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:35.130
Mmm.

387
00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:36.230
There you go.

388
00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:38.270
Good stuff.

389
00:17:39.550 --> 00:17:42.990
Yeah, Pam goes, not the hands.

390
00:17:43.990 --> 00:17:47.150
Lady, he didn't wash his hands after going number one.

391
00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:48.850
Did it make you think of anyone?

392
00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:49.790
I'm sorry.

393
00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:52.830
Men touch their mister parts.

394
00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:54.770
You don't touch your lady, Biz.

395
00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:56.270
No.

396
00:17:56.670 --> 00:18:02.310
Listen, men like handle their penis when they pee, right?

397
00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:04.730
Don't they have to touch it and get it out?

398
00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:06.950
I'm assuming they have to flop it out.

399
00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:08.410
I don't know how, thank you.

400
00:18:08.430 --> 00:18:08.970
Oh, thank you, Sam.

401
00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:10.710
I mean, I don't know exactly how it works.

402
00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:11.850
I don't know the mechanics.

403
00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:18.430
But I think if your hand has touched your bits, you should wash them.

404
00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:22.230
Right, because then basically he just touched the appetizers with penis hand.

405
00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:23.110
Yes.

406
00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:23.610
Yes.

407
00:18:24.070 --> 00:18:24.470
Right.

408
00:18:24.710 --> 00:18:24.950
Okay.

409
00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:28.730
Also, I can't believe I still have to defend this.

410
00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:35.590
I have said that sometimes after going number one in my own house, I do not wash my hands.

411
00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:36.130
I know.

412
00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:41.810
If I'm at someone else's house, if I am in public, if I'm at the airport, if I'm hosting

413
00:18:41.810 --> 00:18:44.130
a dinner party, I wash my hands, everybody.

414
00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:44.990
Do you know?

415
00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:45.270
Okay.

416
00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:53.410
Do you know, I saw a thing that was like, I don't know, it was on, I forget where, BuzzFeed,

417
00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:58.370
one of those kind of things that said like 10 celebrities with gross hygiene happens.

418
00:18:58.390 --> 00:18:58.990
Oh my God.

419
00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:00.070
You are on the liSt.

420
00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:00.670
Am I on the list?

421
00:19:00.710 --> 00:19:01.910
Because of the pee story.

422
00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:02.810
Oh my God.

423
00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:03.570
Oh my God.

424
00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:04.330
I don't know.

425
00:19:04.510 --> 00:19:08.310
It makes me want to get genuinely in love back in the news cycle.

426
00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:10.670
I don't know what's worse.

427
00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:12.310
Oh my gosh.

428
00:19:12.390 --> 00:19:13.030
I'm sorry.

429
00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:17.830
I'm just thankful that Ellie Kemper wrote in her book that she also does not always

430
00:19:17.830 --> 00:19:19.430
wash her hands after number one.

431
00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:21.410
In her own home when she's not hosting.

432
00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:23.050
Is it a St. Louis thing?

433
00:19:23.230 --> 00:19:23.750
Oh Lord.

434
00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:25.530
Don't bring St. Louis into it.

435
00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:26.950
St. Louis is like, don't you dare.

436
00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:28.050
You're going to get mail.

437
00:19:29.170 --> 00:19:31.130
Uh, all right.

438
00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:33.650
Well, I have a fan story from Stephanie M.

439
00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:35.670
in Saskatchewan, Canada.

440
00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:41.770
And this letter, Stephanie, reminded me of my own dinner party horror story that I will

441
00:19:41.770 --> 00:19:42.930
share in a moment.

442
00:19:43.130 --> 00:19:45.690
But here is Stephanie's story.

443
00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:51.030
Stephanie says, this happened more than 10 years ago, and I'm still baffled by the whole

444
00:19:51.030 --> 00:19:51.310
thing.

445
00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:56.370
My boyfriend's best friend was getting married, and rather than having a giant event, the

446
00:19:56.370 --> 00:20:01.430
couple opted for a close friends and family event only, with dinner to be hosted at their

447
00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:01.830
house.

448
00:20:02.290 --> 00:20:07.610
Because my boyfriend was in the bridal party, I was not invited to the ceremony, but I

449
00:20:07.610 --> 00:20:08.950
was invited to the dinner.

450
00:20:09.210 --> 00:20:09.630
Okay.

451
00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:15.050
So I guess the ceremony was just literally family and bridal party.

452
00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:15.410
Okay.

453
00:20:15.570 --> 00:20:17.250
And then the dinner was a bigger thing.

454
00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:17.690
Okay.

455
00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:21.790
I asked my boyfriend, what time should I arrive at the house for dinner?

456
00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:24.010
And I was told 530.

457
00:20:24.510 --> 00:20:24.870
Great.

458
00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:26.350
Stephanie said, no problem.

459
00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:27.230
I can do that.

460
00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:31.550
I like how Stephanie is not even bumped by not being invited to the wedding.

461
00:20:31.550 --> 00:20:34.610
Yeah, she's like, listen, this is his close friends.

462
00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:35.630
I don't really know them.

463
00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:36.110
It's okay.

464
00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:36.910
You do you.

465
00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:39.030
Just tell me when to be there and where.

466
00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:40.070
At the bigger celebration.

467
00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:40.450
Yes.

468
00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:40.690
Yeah.

469
00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:45.110
Stephanie says, I arrived to the house at 520 with a bottle of champagne and the wedding

470
00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:49.010
gift to discover that everyone was already seated at the table waiting for me.

471
00:20:49.230 --> 00:20:49.610
Uh-oh.

472
00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:50.770
I was mortified.

473
00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:55.610
The bride told me it was nice of me to show up and showed me where to sit.

474
00:20:56.050 --> 00:20:56.490
Snark.

475
00:20:56.490 --> 00:21:01.570
I figured it was my mistake and I apologized for being late until my boyfriend confirmed

476
00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:08.230
that he had been told 530 and the bride changed her mind to 5 o'clock at 5 o'clock.

477
00:21:08.510 --> 00:21:12.050
Is she being like a little sabotage-y?

478
00:21:12.150 --> 00:21:13.410
Does she not like Stephanie?

479
00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:14.190
I don't know.

480
00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:18.130
Stephanie says, so we're moving on with dinner and everything's going fine.

481
00:21:18.310 --> 00:21:21.690
And then at 8 o'clock, the bride decides she's done and going to bed.

482
00:21:21.930 --> 00:21:22.790
At 8 o'clock.

483
00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:23.490
At 8 o'clock.

484
00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:27.510
The guests were surprised and started cleaning up and getting ready to leave.

485
00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:31.090
The bride went around the table hugging everyone and saying goodnight.

486
00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:35.550
And since she had always hugged me every time we saw each other, I offered her a congratulations

487
00:21:35.550 --> 00:21:36.310
and a hug.

488
00:21:36.510 --> 00:21:40.990
She rolled her eyes and said, I mean, I guess if you want a hug.

489
00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:42.110
What?

490
00:21:42.550 --> 00:21:44.170
Stephanie said we left shortly after.

491
00:21:44.350 --> 00:21:49.330
It was by far the most bizarre dinner and wedding dinner I've ever experienced.

492
00:21:49.770 --> 00:21:51.750
Stephanie, I have questions about this bride.

493
00:21:51.750 --> 00:21:54.010
I feel like she has a vendetta or something.

494
00:21:54.150 --> 00:21:56.310
She's got her bullseye on you.

495
00:21:56.550 --> 00:21:57.910
Was this bride pregnant?

496
00:21:58.230 --> 00:21:58.630
Or?

497
00:21:58.870 --> 00:22:02.930
Because I just feel like if you're doing a small wedding.

498
00:22:03.250 --> 00:22:04.310
You're going to bed at 8.

499
00:22:04.430 --> 00:22:05.390
Going to bed at 8.

500
00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:07.170
You're a little cranky.

501
00:22:07.830 --> 00:22:08.770
You're annoyed.

502
00:22:08.770 --> 00:22:15.290
Or is it possible that the bride maybe had at one time had a thing for Stephanie's beau?

503
00:22:16.430 --> 00:22:16.830
Wow.

504
00:22:17.410 --> 00:22:17.930
Just saying.

505
00:22:18.610 --> 00:22:19.210
Don't know.

506
00:22:19.550 --> 00:22:20.270
We don't know.

507
00:22:20.390 --> 00:22:20.870
We don't know.

508
00:22:20.990 --> 00:22:23.750
If we had been invited, we could have mom detected it for the moment.

509
00:22:24.770 --> 00:22:26.050
